summary:
- topic: School Board Recognition Month
  text: The board celebrated School Board Recognition Month, honoring board members
    with student artwork and new lapel pins. Student artists were also recognized
    for their contributions to the 'You Belong Here' theme.
- topic: Student Representative Report
  text: Student Representative Gabe Domingos provided updates on high school events,
    athletics, and elementary/middle school activities, including a reminder about
    academic eligibility for extracurriculars. He also announced the upcoming 'Addams
    Family' musical, in which he holds a lead role.
- topic: FY2025 Budget Development
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina reported on the ongoing FY2025 budget
    development process, noting challenges and encouraging community participation
    in upcoming budget workshops in March. A dedicated budget page is available on
    the district website.
- topic: School Safety Initiatives
  text: Updates on school safety included investments in South Portland High School's
    main entrance glass, anticipated consultant reports for Brown School and SPHS,
    and a state proposal for elementary school vestibule security. A new part-time
    security assistant was hired to focus on exterior school security across the district.
- topic: Enrollment and Personnel
  text: Current enrollment stands at 2,933, showing stabilization after previous fluctuations,
    though a potential loss of students is anticipated due to changes in temporary
    housing. The consent agenda included the election of Lindsey Hutchins as Behavior
    Strategist for Small School and noted no resignations or retirements for the second
    consecutive month.
- topic: Policy Approvals and Rescissions
  text: The board approved several policies, including those related to tobacco-free
    schools (Policy ADC), physical restraint and seclusion (Policies JKAA and JKAA-R),
    and resignation of school unit employees (Policy GCQC). Several outdated policies
    were also rescinded as part of the consent agenda.
- topic: Financial Health and Donations
  text: The Finance Committee reported a healthy budget status, with 46.3% of the
    year's budget spent. The board accepted various donations and grants from organizations
    like the Rotary Club, High Roller Lobster, Hannaford Helps Schools, Teens to Trails,
    and Pike Industries, supporting school programs and student wellness.
- topic: Community Input on Reconfiguration
  text: A citizen, Julia Edwards, urged board members to thoroughly review all available
    resources on school boundaries and configurations in preparation for upcoming
    discussions, emphasizing the importance of informed decision-making.
